# Windows Driver Frameworks (KMDF 1.17) — our delta from pristine upstream.
#
# Upstream: https://github.com/microsoft/Windows-Driver-Frameworks at tag win-10.0.10586.0
#           (Windows 10 1511). Only src/framework/ is vendored — all 475 of its files,
#           nothing skipped. src/publicinc/ (156 files) is NOT vendored at all.
#
# APPLYING THIS PATCH TAKES TWO STEPS, and the first one is not optional:
#
#     tar xf <upstream>; cd <upstream>/src/framework
#     find . -type f -exec sed -i 's/[ \t\r]*$//' {} +      # <-- NORMALIZE FIRST
#     patch -p1 < vendor-patches/wdf.patch
#
# That reproduces sdk/lib/drivers/wdf byte-for-byte (verified: 0 differences, 0 fuzz,
# 0 rejects), modulo the seven files that have no upstream counterpart at all —
# CMakeLists.txt, VENDORED, reactos_special.{cpp,h}, wdf01000.rc, wdf01000_reg.inf and
# LICENSE (which is upstream's, just from the repo root rather than from src/framework).
#
# WHY THE sed. Our copy has ZERO trailing whitespace anywhere in 477 files, which the
# repo's .editorconfig (trim_trailing_whitespace = true, applied to [*]) will keep
# stripping. Upstream has it all over the place. That single difference accounts for
# 85% OF THE APPARENT DELTA:
#
#     raw diff vs pristine:            395 files, 34,224 changed lines
#     after stripping trailing WS:     263 files,  5,411 changed lines
#
# 132 files differ from upstream by NOTHING BUT trailing whitespace. Folding that into
# a documented, deterministic preprocessing step rather than into the patch is what
# makes this artifact reviewable at 420 KB instead of 2.4 MB. It also means a re-vendor
# should diff with `-w`, or it will read 34k lines of churn as a port.
#
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT THE REMAINING 5,411 LINES ARE
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#     1,252   155 files   #include path and case: backslashes to forward slashes, and
#                         filename case fixed for a case-sensitive filesystem
#     1,197    18 files   comments
#     1,049    84 files   NTAPI / WDFAPI / __declspec / calling-convention annotations
#                         added for clang and GCC
#       989    75 files   everything else — see the concentrations below
#       401    49 files   blank lines
#       178    89 files   WPP `#include "Foo.tmh"` commented out (we have no WPP)
#       142    57 files   preprocessor
#       122    42 files   `__super::` rewritten to the explicit base class
#        62    29 files   explicitly marked `reactos` blocks
#        19     5 files   ROSWDFNOTIMPLEMENTED
#
# Nearly all of it is mechanical portability. The substance is concentrated in four
# files: poxinterface.cpp (228 lines — the Power Framework interop, stubbed out behind
# ROSWDFNOTIMPLEMENTED), fxpkgpnp.cpp (166), and the KM halves fxpkgpnpkm.cpp (92) and
# fxpkgfdokm.cpp (62).
#
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NO UNMARKED FUNCTIONAL REMOVALS REMAIN — CHECKED, NOT ASSUMED
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The whole delta was scanned for files whose diff nets out to removed or commented-out
# executable code while containing no `reactos` and no ROSWDFNOTIMPLEMENTED anywhere.
# Six files matched, and all six are benign on inspection:
#
#   fxpkgio.cpp             `(UCHAR)DispatchContext` -> `(UCHAR)(ULONG_PTR)DispatchContext`
#                           in two ASSERTs. A genuine portability FIX; casting a pointer
#                           straight to UCHAR is ill-formed on a 64-bit clang. Also drops
#                           `__inline` from two __fastcall definitions.
#   fxioqueuekm.cpp         `RtlZeroMemory(m_FwdProgContext, sizeof(...))` -> `*m_FwdProgContext = {}`.
#                           Equivalent.
#   fxtelemetry.cpp         Include case, plus a comment ending in a bare `\` — which is a
#                           line continuation that would swallow the following line. Also a fix.
#   pdopower.cpp, fxchildlist.cpp, fxiotarget.cpp
#                           declare-at-top merged into declare-at-use; net-negative line
#                           counts, no behaviour.
#
# The ONE real unmarked removal this tree used to carry — powerstatemachinekm.cpp
# silently skipping the DMA-enabler PowerUp()/PowerDown() loops in both device power
# transitions — was found and RESTORED on 2026-09-20, before this patch was taken. It is
# therefore not in here, which is the point.
#
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TWO THINGS THIS PATCH DOES NOT COVER
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# THE LOADER IS A SEPARATE TREE, DELIBERATELY. wdf01000 still puts
# sdk/lib/drivers/wdfldr on its include path and does `add_importlibs(wdf01000 wdfldr)`.
# That is how KMDF works — the framework binds to a loader, and upstream's drop does not
# contain WdfLdr.sys or WdfDriverEntry.lib. Ours are ReactOS-authored GPL-2.0-or-later
# reimplementations and live at sdk/lib/drivers/{wdfldr,wdfdriverentry}, outside this
# vendored boundary, along with three ReactOS headers in wdf_reactos/include/. An
# upstream re-vendor still needs them supplied beside it.
#
# 101 VENDORED FILES ARE NEVER BUILT: umdf/ (10 files) and shared/*/um/ (91), since
# CMakeLists builds wdf01000 from SOURCE_SHARED + SOURCE_KM only. They are in this patch
# because they are in the tree, but nothing here compiles them, so their delta has never
# been exercised by anything.
#
# THE GITHUB TARBALL HASH IS NOT A PROVENANCE ANCHOR. This registry once recorded
# sha256 6289cf8b5284ab27a801f7a04d9bb35c893159e82c04055df079e3ab3dcb3304 for the
# archive; refetching the same tag on 2026-09-20 gave
# d252fc80175bb249a278ea284a887ec201220f709bf04b110f1afc3fdb6a4b31. GitHub's
# auto-generated archives are not byte-stable, so the tag is the identifier and the
# round-trip above is the check — not the tarball hash.
#
